!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Absorption cross-section N2O5: N2O5 + hv --> NO3 + NO2
! source : JPL-2006 (identical in JPL-2011) for T-indep part (i.e. wl<285 and wl>380nm)
!          JPL-2002 for T-dependent part encoded in CRS_TDEP
! i.e. T-indep part comes from http://www.atmosphere.mpg.de/enid/2295
!                 -> Catalogue -> "Nitrogen oxides" -> "N2O5" -> "JPL-2006"
! Rem1: Quantum yield = 1.
! Rem2: Temperature influence:   
!   i)  200-281nm: T indep. The provided crs values come from JPL-2006 (195-298K).
!   ii) 285-380nm: T dep. according to the formula (JPL-2002):
!           10^20 * crs = exp{2.735 + ((4278.5 - 17.127*wl)/T)}
!       The cross sections are computed in subroutine CRS_TDEP.
!       Accordingly, the "285-380nm" values provided below are not used
!       to compute the table of photodissociation constants.
!       WARNING: this param is obsolete, was updated in JPL-2006(=JPL-2011)
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        60  | Finishes at wl interval :  108
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!  no  from(nm) to(nm)  | crs (cm2) | qyield (0->1) |   Tdep_param1 |   Tdep_param2
